window.STUDY={"id":"ap-26-sun-print","code":"AP-26","title":"Sun print · a year of daylight at 60° N","fig":"4.26","kicker":"Application · 26","lede":"A bar chart made by the sun.","body":["Twelve strips of card, cut to the hours of daylight at 60° north on the 15th of each month, were laid on brushed cyanotype paper with the cut-out title and month letters, and a cotton thread marks 12 hours. Where the card lay flat the edge is sharp; where it curled the shadow went soft. The plate number is typed in the margin."],"source":"Made with the effect set: Cyanotype, Typewriter strike, Paper tooth.","ref":{"w":1500,"h":1000},"variants":[{"id":"set","label":"As drawn","sw":[]}],"points":[],"colorHint":"The inks are dials of the effects: open Parameters and pick an effect.","paramsHint":"Every dial of the effects this piece uses.","spec":{"usage":{"id":"u-sunprint","job":"data","title":"Sun print · a year of daylight at 60° N","aspect":"3/2","uses":["fx-11-cyanotype","fx-07-typewriter","fx-03-paper-tooth"]},"reference":{"grammar":"A bar chart made by the sun. Twelve strips of card, cut to the hours of daylight at 60° north on the 15th of each month, were laid on brushed cyanotype paper with the cut-out title and month letters, and a cotton thread marks 12 hours. Where the card lay flat the edge is sharp; where it curled the shadow went soft. The plate number is typed in the margin."},"techniques":[{"id":"fx-11-cyanotype","name":"Cyanotype","short":"FX-11","atoms":["deposit","expose"],"params":{"dieSize":{"value":0.72,"range":[0.2,1],"label":"Motif size","step":0.01,"note":"motif height as a share of the plate"},"strokes":{"value":4,"range":[2,8],"label":"Brush strokes","step":1,"note":"strokes laid top to bottom, alternating direction"},"bAngle":{"value":-1.5,"range":[-30,30],"label":"Brush angle","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"tilt of the brush strokes"},"brushRag":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Brush-edge raggedness","step":0.01,"note":"how far bristles and drag push each stroke edge in and out"},"uneven":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Coating unevenness","step":0.01,"note":"streaks and drag in the sensitizer thickness"},"dry":{"value":0.3,"range":[0,1],"label":"Dry-brush tails","step":0.01,"note":"how far the load runs out before the brush lifts: bristle streaks on the tooth peaks"},"pool":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Pooling","step":0.01,"note":"sensitizer beading where the brush lands and stops, and the drying rim along each edge"},"expo":{"value":1.25,"range":[0.2,3],"label":"Exposure","step":0.01,"note":"sun dose; 1 = full development of an unshaded coat"},"lift":{"value":3,"range":[0,24],"label":"Object lift","step":0.1,"unit":"px","note":"height of the lifted parts above the sheet. It sets the penumbra width and its offset away from the sheet light"},"contact":{"value":0.6,"range":[0,1],"label":"Contact","step":0.01,"note":"share of the subject pressed flat (sharp); the rest curls up (soft)"},"scatter":{"value":0.3,"range":[0.05,1],"label":"Sky scatter","step":0.01,"note":"penumbra per px of lift: skylight and haze around the sun"},"trans":{"value":0,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Translucency","step":0.005,"note":"UV passing through leaf tissue (cut card: 0)"},"bleed":{"value":0.3,"range":[0,1],"label":"Wash bleed","step":0.01,"note":"Prussian blue carried downhill into the whites during the wash, in streaks"},"density":{"value":1.45,"range":[0.3,2],"label":"Film density","step":0.01,"note":"film density of a fully exposed coat (Beer–Lambert: deeper and more saturated)"},"cL":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,1],"label":"Custom tone · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"cC":{"value":0.12,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Custom tone · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"ch":{"value":256,"range":[0,360],"label":"Custom tone · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"seed":{"value":23,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Coating = brush strokes in stroke space (along s, across t): a load that runs out along the stroke; edges displaced by per-side noise (raggedness); a set-down pool and a drying rim; bristle streaks × the stock height decide where a dry brush still deposits. Thickness τ = load × unevenness (streaks + low-frequency drag) + pools; overlapping strokes add (a double coat prints deeper); paper valleys hold more sensitizer. Objects (procedural fern frond, grass with spikelets, or a cut-card motif) are an AA clip. Lift = a smooth field × the lift dial; contact sets how much lies flat. Shadow: for each lift level z the clip is sampled toward the sheet light at z · cot(elevation) (smeared ±20 % along the light) and blurred by z × sky scatter; each pixel blends the two levels around its lift. Exposure E = 1 − shadow × (1 − translucency). Develop: r = ((1 − e^(−2.2·exposure·E)) ÷ (1 − e^(−2.2)))^1.35, capped at 1.2; the coat saturates as τ' = 1.3·(1 − e^(−τ/1.3)); density = τ' × (a faint stain + r) × film density. Overexposure fills the penumbra in. Wash: unexposed coating rinses away; Prussian blue bleeds a little downhill into the whites, in streaks. Color = Beer–Lambert film of the tone (fresh, classic, peroxide-oxidized, tea-toned). Light last: × the stock's shading under the sheet light.","limits":"object lift > 18 px: penumbra wider than the leaflets: the fern dissolves into a cloud. exposure > 2.5: penumbra fills in; fine pinnules and awns vanish. exposure < .5: pale, greenish print: reads as underexposed. raggedness > .8: stroke edges tear into islands. strokes > 6: brush marks shrink into stripes"},{"id":"fx-07-typewriter","name":"Typewriter strike","short":"FX-07","atoms":["transfer","deform"],"params":{"fsize":{"value":34,"range":[8,48],"label":"Size","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"type size in CSS px; bold below 15 px"},"lead":{"value":1.5,"range":[1,2.4],"label":"Leading","step":0.01,"note":"line spacing as a multiple of the size"},"vari":{"value":0.18,"range":[0,1],"label":"Key variance","step":0.01,"note":"how unevenly keys strike"},"half":{"value":0.05,"range":[0,0.4],"label":"Half strikes","step":0.005,"note":"share of glyphs where only the top or bottom lands"},"jx":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,2],"label":"Jitter x","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"horizontal offset per strike"},"jy":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,2],"label":"Jitter y","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"vertical offset per strike"},"rot":{"value":0.7,"range":[0,4],"label":"Rotation","step":0.05,"unit":"°","note":"rotation spread per strike"},"exhaust":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ribbon wear","step":0.01,"note":"ink fading along the text"},"ribbon":{"value":0.5,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ribbon texture","step":0.01,"note":"how much the ribbon weave shows in the glyphs"},"rcount":{"value":95,"range":[20,200],"label":"Ribbon count","step":1,"unit":"/100px","note":"ribbon threads per 100 CSS px"},"squash":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ink squash","step":0.01,"note":"film pooling at the glyph edge"},"impress":{"value":0.25,"range":[0,1],"label":"Press depth","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"how deep each strike dents the stock"},"diffuse":{"value":0.7,"range":[0,1],"label":"Diffuse share","step":0.01,"note":"share of light from the sheet light vs flat ambient fill"},"bite":{"value":0.55,"range":[0,1],"label":"Stock bite","step":0.01,"note":"how much the stock height (vs film-splitting noise) decides where ink lands"},"breakup":{"value":0.85,"range":[0,1],"label":"Break-up ↔ thin","step":0.01,"note":"1 = ink film breaks into marks on the peaks as pressure falls; 0 = the film stays whole and thins to tone"},"starve":{"value":0.03,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Starve","step":0.002,"note":"the lowest share of the surface never takes ink. Pinholes in the solid, placed by the paper's valleys and pits"},"wick":{"value":0.12,"range":[0,1],"label":"Wick","step":0.01,"note":"ink carried along fibers into the run-out (hairline feathering)"},"mottle":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,1],"label":"Mottle","step":0.01,"note":"paper formation (its low-frequency cloudiness) varying the film thickness"},"split":{"value":0.8,"range":[0.5,10],"label":"Film split","step":0.1,"unit":"px","note":"clump size of the film-splitting noise (the roller's own speckle)"},"iL":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ink · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"iC":{"value":0.006,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Ink · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"ih":{"value":280,"range":[0,360],"label":"Ink · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"density":{"value":1.15,"range":[0.2,2],"label":"Film thickness","step":0.01,"note":"ink film at full pressure (Beer–Lambert)"},"seed":{"value":7,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Text in Courier Prime (a typewriter slab; bold below 15 px, as a light strike loses thin strokes), one strike per glyph on the main thread: pressure = ribbon life (exhausting along the page) × key variance; offset, rotation, an occasional dropped baseline; a half strike is a linear pressure ramp across the glyph, fading top or bottom. Ribbon: a plain weave at the ribbon count. Ink transfers through thread crossings, less through the gaps. Ink chain: pressure × ribbon vs stock-height percentile; ink squash pools film at the glyph edge. Impression: the strike dents the stock (blurred glyph × pressure); light from the combined height. Color: Beer–Lambert film.","limits":"ribbon count < 30 /100 px: weave reads as a screen pattern on the type. jitter > 1.5 px: reads as broken font rendering. size < 7 px: strokes thinner than the tooth lose the ribbon texture"},{"id":"fx-03-paper-tooth","name":"Paper tooth","short":"FX-03","atoms":["form"],"params":{"scale":{"value":4,"range":[0.5,24],"label":"Tooth scale","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"feature size of the tooth (noise wavelength), not a tile zoom"},"oct":{"value":4,"range":[1,6],"label":"Octaves","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"layers of finer detail"},"fibers":{"value":3,"range":[0,40],"label":"Fibers","step":0.25,"unit":"/100×100 px","note":"laid fibers per 100 × 100 CSS px"},"fLen":{"value":14,"range":[2,80],"label":"Fiber length","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"mean fiber length"},"fWidth":{"value":0.4,"range":[0.2,3],"label":"Fiber width","step":0.02,"unit":"px","note":"mean fiber width"},"pits":{"value":0.5,"range":[0,40],"label":"Pits","step":0.25,"unit":"/100×100 px","note":"depressions per 100 × 100 CSS px"},"pers":{"value":0.42,"range":[0.15,0.85],"label":"Persistence","step":0.01,"note":"amplitude kept per octave: the spectral dropoff of the tooth"},"aniso":{"value":1.4,"range":[1,6],"label":"Anisotropy","step":0.05,"note":"tooth stretched along the grain angle. Machine-made paper is never isotropic; 1 = the 1999 \"paper\" filter look"},"form":{"value":0.3,"range":[0,1],"label":"Formation","step":0.01,"note":"low-frequency cloudiness of the sheet (fiber flocs); also mottles any ink printed on it"},"formScale":{"value":60,"range":[10,200],"label":"Formation scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"size of the flocs"},"fAngle":{"value":6,"range":[0,180],"label":"Grain angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"machine direction of the fibers and the tooth"},"fSpread":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,1],"label":"Grain spread","step":0.01,"note":"0 = all fibers on the grain; 1 = any direction"},"depth":{"value":0.07,"range":[0,1.6],"label":"Relief","step":0.005,"unit":"px","note":"height of the tooth in CSS px: how hard the light can rake it. The slider is weighted to the subtle end."},"diffuse":{"value":0.55,"range":[0,1],"label":"Diffuse share","step":0.01,"note":"share of light from the sheet light vs flat ambient fill"},"fRaise":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fiber raise","step":0.01,"note":"how far fibers stand proud of the sheet"},"pDepth":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,1],"label":"Pit depth","step":0.01,"note":"how deep pits go"},"paperL":{"value":0.968,"range":[0.85,1],"label":"Paper L","step":0.001,"note":"OKLab lightness of the stock under the sheet light. Below 1 so lit walls, foil and sheen have headroom to brighten; 1 = the white of the page (highlights clip)"},"fDark":{"value":0.014,"range":[0,0.15],"label":"Fiber tone","step":0.001,"unit":"ΔL","note":"albedo darkening of fibers"},"pDark":{"value":0.02,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Pit tone","step":0.001,"unit":"ΔL","note":"albedo darkening in pits"},"tL":{"value":0.7,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fill tint · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"tC":{"value":0,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Fill tint · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"th":{"value":250,"range":[0,360],"label":"Fill tint · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"tAmt":{"value":0.5,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fill tint amount","step":0.01,"note":"how much the ambient fill takes the tint (shadows go cool / warm)"},"mInset":{"value":22,"range":[0,120],"label":"Inset","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"distance from the plate edge to the mask edge"},"mAmp":{"value":2.5,"range":[0,40],"label":"Edge wander","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far noise pushes the edge in and out"},"mScale":{"value":28,"range":[4,240],"label":"Wander scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander; small = ragged, large = drifting"},"mRough":{"value":5,"range":[1,6],"label":"Roughness","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"octaves of edge noise: adds fine teeth without moving the large shape"},"mFeather":{"value":1.2,"range":[0.5,60],"label":"Feather","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"width over which coverage falls from 1 to 0"},"lift":{"value":1,"range":[0,4],"label":"Sheet lift","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"thickness / curl of the sheet: sizes its shadow on the page"},"mBite":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Bite","step":0.01,"note":"clumped dropouts that grow more likely toward the edge"},"seed":{"value":21,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Height = fbm at the tooth scale (octaves, persistence = how fast detail drops off), reshaped by the distribution curve; blended with low-frequency formation. Fibers: curved capsules at a count per 100 × 100 CSS px near the grain angle, raised into the height; pits: small depressions. Both also darken the albedo slightly. Normal from the height gradient → Lambert under the sheet light (azimuth + elevation from the light puck). Diffuse share vs ambient fill; the fill can be tinted. The same field is the stock for FX-01 and FX-02: its peaks take ink first, its valleys starve, its fibers wick. Mask = the sheet's cut or deckle edge; the sheet casts a contact + ambient shadow onto the page by the same light.","limits":"relief > .6 px: reads as stucco: the stock-filter emboss look. anisotropy < 1.3: isotropic tooth reads as a 1999 paper filter. tooth scale < .8 px: collapses into per-pixel noise: digital grain. fibers > 30 /100×100 px: felt, not paper. light elevation < 15°: every fiber becomes a hard ridge; ok for a raking-light study, not for a page"}],"pass_order":["Cyanotype · A sun print.","Typewriter strike · Each glyph is a separate strike: its own pressure, a slight offset and rotation, sometimes only half the face lands.","Paper tooth · White stock that is not a screen."]}};
